    pr_ref:  # ddaf
    description: "**Defect.** The `evidence_spans` edge field is declared and marked done, but no producer ever populates it.\n\n**Evidence.** `evidence_spans` is declared on the Edge dataclass (ir.py:612), documented in spec §812 as structured evidence locations, and listed under a passing schema-validation test (spec line 1530, \"Required field presence (... evidence_spans)\"). Yet it is absent from 100% of edges (0/110533). `to_dict` writes it only when non-null (ir.py:733) and no producer ever passes a value. The backing test `test_edge_has_evidence_spans` (test_ir.py:607) asserts only a constructor round-trip, not that any real producer emits it — so the done-status claim is satisfied by a round-trip while production coverage is 0%. A fresh run yields a calls edge with no evidence_spans.\n\n**Contract.** A field documented as carrying structured evidence locations and listed under a passing required-field-presence check should be populated by some producer.\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer following the spec to read structured evidence locations off any edge gets nothing on every edge — the delivered-status claim does not match production reality."  # ddaf
    fields: {}  # ddaf
- op: discuss  # b7a8
